@db @compare
Feature: Cross-source data comparison # app/features/data_compare.feature:2
  As a data engineer
  I want to compare recordsets between databases, Excel files, APIs and the UI
  So that migrations and pipelines move data without loss or corruption
  @demo
  Scenario: Customers in the database match the Excel extract                 # app/features/data_compare.feature:8
    Given the compare config "app/datasets/compare/customers_db_vs_excel.yml" # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:41
    When I run the data comparison                                            # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:48
    Then the source and target row counts should match                        # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:69
    And there should be no duplicate primary keys in the source               # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:90
    And there should be no records missing in the target                      # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:76
    And there should be no records missing in the source                      # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:83
    And there should be no field mismatches                                   # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:106

  @demo
  Scenario Outline: Compare configs can be batched with one overall assertion -- @1.1   # app/features/data_compare.feature:25
    Given the compare config "app/datasets/compare/customers_db_vs_excel.yml"           # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:41
    When I run the data comparison                                                      # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:48
    Then the data comparison should pass                                                # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:140

  @demo
  Scenario: Known differences stay within the agreed tolerance                      # app/features/data_compare.feature:28
    Given the compare config "app/datasets/compare/customers_db_vs_excel_diffs.yml" # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:41
    When I run the data comparison                                                  # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:48
    Then the field "NAME" should have no mismatches                                 # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:119
    And the field "STATUS" should have no mismatches                                # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:119
    And the mismatch percentage should be at most 15                                # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:132

  @demo_fail
  Scenario: Customers with known differences are detected                           # app/features/data_compare.feature:36
    Given the compare config "app/datasets/compare/customers_db_vs_excel_diffs.yml" # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:41
    When I run the data comparison                                                  # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:48
    Then there should be no records missing in the target                           # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:76
      ASSERT FAILED: No records missing in target: expected 0; actual 1. Keys present in source but absent in target

    And there should be no field mismatches                                         # None

