@db @validation
Feature: Table data sanity validation # app/features/data_validation.feature:2
  As a data steward
  I want to run sanity checks on a table or query result
  So that bad data is caught early
  @demo
  Scenario: Clean ORDERS data passes every sanity check                    # app/features/data_validation.feature:8
    Given the validation config "app/datasets/validation/orders_clean.yml" # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:185
    When I run the data validations                                        # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:192
    Then all validations should pass                                       # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:211

  @demo
  Scenario: Individual check groups can be asserted separately             # app/features/data_validation.feature:14
    Given the validation config "app/datasets/validation/orders_clean.yml" # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:185
    When I run the data validations                                        # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:192
    Then all "not_null" validations should pass                            # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:216
    And all "numeric" validations should pass                              # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:216
    And the validation "no_orphan_orders" should pass                      # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:223

  @demo_fail
  Scenario: Dirty ORDERS data is flagged                                   # app/features/data_validation.feature:22
    Given the validation config "app/datasets/validation/orders_dirty.yml" # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:185
    When I run the data validations                                        # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:192
    Then all validations should pass                                       # pyassure/steps/data_steps.py:211
      ASSERT FAILED: 7 validation(s) failed - see report


